            "6. Abstract Submission",
            "6. Abstract, Submission and File Upload",
            @"
<p>
Users may submit abstracts or papers for congresses for which they are registered. Users are responsible for the accuracy
of submission titles, abstract texts, keywords, author information, presentation type and uploaded files.
</p>

<ul>
    <li>The submitted academic content must belong to the user or the necessary permissions must have been obtained.</li>
    <li>Plagiarism, fabricated data, misleading information or unauthorized content sharing is prohibited.</li>
    <li>Author information must be accurate and up to date.</li>
    <li>If co-author information is entered, it is assumed that the necessary knowledge and consent of those persons exists.</li>
    <li>File uploads must comply with the format and size limits set by the system.</li>
    <li>Submissions that do not comply with congress formatting rules may be rejected by the organizer or scientific committee.</li>
</ul>

<p>
Accepted submissions may be used in congress programs, abstract books, acceptance letters, participation documents or academic publication processes.
</p>"
